-// Chapter 32 checkpoint 4: the weight, and the colour half of the order-independent accumulation.
+// Chapter 32 checkpoint 5: the frame measures how wrong each approximation is.
 //
-// A weighted blended fragment carries a confidence, not a second opacity, which is why the weight is a function of
-// depth alone and why the fragment's alpha enters the accumulation separately and exactly once. The weight is
-// clamped: an unbounded weight would let one fragment win the average outright and turn the technique into an
-// expensive, order-independent way of drawing the nearest fragment.
+// Three composites have existed since checkpoint 1 and none of them has said anything about the others. ComposeCS
+// now publishes the four numbers that let a reader rank them: the largest per-channel difference between the
+// order-independent composite and the sorted reference, the difference in scene luminance between them, the
+// difference in layer alpha between them - which is where the claim that weighted blended coverage is exact stops
+// being a claim - and the largest per-channel difference between the per-draw composite and the sorted reference.
 //
-// OitAccumulateCS now adds each fragment's weighted premultiplied colour and its weighted alpha into whichever
-// accumulator it is visiting, so the resolve finally has a colour to average and its epsilon guard stops firing
-// wherever the layer is present. The revealage the stage has accumulated since checkpoint 2 does not change, which
-// is the point: the coverage was already exact, and it is the colour that is the approximation.
+// The frame also stops assuming its accumulators are safe. A pixel whose candidate count exceeds the authored pane
+// table or whose weighted alpha sum exceeds the declared bound raises an overflow flag, and the frame publishes the
+// maximum of every error, of the reactive mask and of the weighted alpha sum as float bit patterns, which order
+// identically to the non-negative floats themselves.

 #include "../Common/TransparencyShared.hlsli"

@@ -852,6 +853,13 @@ bool EarlierSubmitted(uint leftDrawOrder, uint leftSlot, uint rightDrawOrder, ui
     float3 objectOver = float3(record.objectOverR, record.objectOverG, record.objectOverB);
     float3 oitOver = float3(record.oitOverR, record.oitOverG, record.oitOverB);

+    // The approximation evidence. Nothing here claims the weighted blended path is exact; these are the numbers that
+    // say by how much it is not, and the order error beside them says the same about the cheaper per-draw order.
+    record.oitChannelError = MaximumChannel(abs(oitOver - sortedOver));
+    record.oitLuminanceError = abs(SceneLuminance(oitOver) - SceneLuminance(sortedOver));
+    record.oitAlphaError = abs(record.oitLayerAlpha - record.sortedLayerAlpha);
+    record.orderChannelError = MaximumChannel(abs(objectOver - sortedOver));
+
     float3 composite = sortedOver;
     if (CompositeModeId == CompositeObjectSorted)
     {
@@ -921,7 +929,8 @@ bool EarlierSubmitted(uint leftDrawOrder, uint leftSlot, uint rightDrawOrder, ui
     Records[index] = record;

